Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: upstream, https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/ffmpeg.git/commit/cb746137ed0dd2bc950cff109b3374c74bbc2514
From cb746137ed0dd2bc950cff109b3374c74bbc2514 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:55:22 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 42/48] avformat/mpegtsenc: write ISO/IEC 23002-3 auxiliary
 video streams

Write a video stream with AV_PKT_DATA_AUXILIARY_VIDEO_INFO, coded with a
codec that ISO/IEC 13818-1 Table 2-34 gives a stream type, as an
auxiliary video stream: stream type 0x1E, with an auxiliary video stream
descriptor (2.6.74) that names the coding and carries the auxiliary video
SI message in its si_rbsp(), followed by rbsp_trailing_bits().

The mpegts_flags flag omit_si_trailing_bits writes si_rbsp() without
them, as TSDuck reads and writes it: ISO/IEC 23002-3 is not freely
available to settle which form it specifies.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 via Claude Code
---
Refreshed for FFmpeg 9.1 (deb-multimedia 10:9.1-dmo1), 2026-11-26: FFmpeg 9.1 dropped avlanguage.o from the muxer's object line; mpegauxvideo.o is added to 9.1's line.

diff --git a/doc/muxers.texi b/doc/muxers.texi
index a2489760fcd9d95cc8eda1371b1d29e4f3ddaf5e..bce5d80ab012c4d29015323da3844017d8d68a90 100644
--- a/doc/muxers.texi
+++ b/doc/muxers.texi
@@ -3298,8 +3298,18 @@ Mark the initial packet of each stream as discontinuity.
 Emit NIT table.
 @item omit_rai
 Disable writing of random access indicator.
+@item omit_si_trailing_bits
+Write the supplemental information of ISO/IEC 23002-3 auxiliary video streams
+(@code{si_rbsp()} in their auxiliary video stream descriptor) without
+@code{rbsp_trailing_bits()}, as TSDuck reads and writes it.
 @end table
 
+A video stream with @code{AV_PKT_DATA_AUXILIARY_VIDEO_INFO} side data, a depth
+or parallax map for another video stream, is written as an ISO/IEC 23002-3
+auxiliary video stream: stream type 0x1E, with an auxiliary video stream
+descriptor that names its coding and carries the side data (ISO/IEC 13818-1
+2.6.74).
+
 @item mpegts_copyts @var{boolean}
 Preserve original timestamps, if value is set to @code{1}. Default value
 is @code{-1}, which results in shifting timestamps so that they start from 0.
